---
.title = "Settings store",
.description = "A thread-safe JSON key-value file for the app's settings, written atomically, in the app's config directory on every platform.",
.date = .date("2026-10-12T00:00:00"),
.authors = ["Oriel"],
.layout = "docs.shtml",
---

`oriel.store` keeps small settings (a theme, a zoom level, the last folder
opened, a launch counter) in a JSON file the app's Zig code reads and
writes by key. Every change is saved at once, atomically, so a crash or a
power cut leaves either the old file or the new one, never half of each.
Oriel itself uses it to remember window sizes
(`WindowOptions.remember_geometry`).

Use it for settings: a few kilobytes of values the app reads at start.
Use [SQL]($link.page('docs/sql')) for records that grow (notes, history,
anything you query), and plain files under
[`oriel.paths.appData`]($link.page('docs/paths')) for blobs (images,
downloaded models). A setting only the page needs can stay in the page's
`localStorage`; the store is for what Zig needs too.

# [Availability]($heading.id('availability'))

| Platform | Settings file | Atomic write | Lock |
|---|---|---|---|
| Linux | `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/<app id>/<name>.json` (`~/.config/...`) | GLib `g_file_set_contents` | `GMutex` |
| Windows | `%APPDATA%\<app id>\<name>.json` (Roaming) | temp file, `FlushFileBuffers`, `MoveFileExW` (replace existing, write through) | `SRWLOCK` |
| macOS | `~/Library/Application Support/<app id>/<name>.json` | temp file (`O_EXCL`, `0600`), `fsync`, `rename`, directory `fsync` | pthread mutex |
| iOS | `<container>/Library/Application Support/<app id>/<name>.json` | as macOS | pthread mutex |
| Android | `<filesDir>/<app id>/<name>.json` (`/data/user/0/<package>/files/...`) | as macOS | pthread mutex |

The module is on by default on every platform (`store` flag); turn it off
with `.store = false` on the Oriel dependency. It needs no permission.
`oriel.store.available` is `false` when it is off, and then any other
`oriel.store` declaration is a build error unless the use is guarded by
`if (oriel.store.available)`.

# [Quick start]($heading.id('quick-start'))

```zig
// build.zig: the store is on by default; nothing to add.
const dep = b.dependency("oriel", .{ .target = target, .optimize = optimize });
```

```zig
// src/main.zig
const std = @import("std");
const oriel = @import("oriel");
const app = @import("oriel_app");

pub const Commands = struct {
    /// invoke("launches"): counts the app's launches across restarts.
    pub fn launches(_: std.mem.Allocator) !i64 {
        var store = try oriel.store.Store.open(std.heap.smp_allocator, app.build.id, "settings");
        defer store.deinit();
        const n = (store.getInt("launches", i64) orelse 0) + 1;
        try store.set("launches", n); // saved to settings.json now
        return n;
    }
};

pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !u8 {
    return oriel.main(init, .{ .commands = Commands, .events = struct {} }, .{
        .app = app.build,
        .window = .{ .title = "My App", .width = 800, .height = 600 },
    });
}
```

```js
const n = await window.oriel.invoke("launches");
document.title = `Launched ${n} times`;
```

The page has no store API of its own: it reaches the store through the
app's [commands]($link.page('docs/commands')), which decide what the page may
read and change.

# [How it works]($heading.id('how-it-works'))

>[]($block.attrs("mermaid"))
```
flowchart LR
  Page["Page"] -->|"invoke(command)"| Cmd["Your command<br/>(any thread)"]
  Zig["Your Zig code"] --> Store
  Cmd --> Store["Store<br/>(mutex + JSON map<br/>in an arena)"]
  Store -->|"open: read + parse"| File[("config dir/name.json")]
  Store -->|"set / delete / clear / save:<br/>whole file, temp + rename"| File
  Store -.->|"unparseable file:<br/>copy kept"| Corrupt[("name.json.corrupt")]
```

`Store.open(gpa, app_id, name)` resolves the app's config directory
(`configDir`, created if missing), reads `<name>.json` and parses it into a
`std.json.ObjectMap` whose keys and values live in the store's arena. A
missing or empty file is an empty store. A file that doesn't parse is
copied to `<name>.json.corrupt` before anything else, a warning is logged,
and the store opens empty: the next save replaces the original, the copy
keeps the user's data.

Every method takes the store's mutex, so one `*Store` can be shared between
threads (commands run on the main thread, or on workers when listed in
`async_commands`). Each `set` turns the value into JSON and parses it back
into the arena, so the store never borrows the caller's memory. With
`auto_save` on (the default), `set`, `delete` and `clear` rewrite the whole
file before returning; `deinit` saves once more and frees everything.

The file is written atomically: a sibling temp file
(`<name>.json.tmp.<pid>.<n>`), flushed to disk, renamed over the old one
(on macOS, iOS and Android the directory is `fsync`ed too, so the rename
itself survives a power cut). The JSON is indented with two spaces, so it
can be read and edited by hand while the app is closed.

The store is a cache of the file taken at `open`: two `Store`s on the same
file don't see each other's changes, and the last save wins. Open one per
file and keep it, or open, change and close it in one go as the quick start
does.

The code is `src/modules/store.zig` (the facade),
`src/modules/store/common.zig` (`GenericStore`, the JSON logic and the app
id rules) and one backend per platform: `linux.zig` (GLib),
`windows.zig` (Known Folders, Win32 files), `macos.zig` (macOS and iOS,
`$HOME/Library/...`), `android.zig` (the directories the Kotlin runtime
hands over before `main`), with `posix.zig` holding the file and mutex code
macOS, iOS and Android share.

# [Examples]($heading.id('examples'))

## [Keep one store for the app's lifetime]($heading.id('example-shared'))

```zig
const std = @import("std");
const oriel = @import("oriel");
const app = @import("oriel_app");

var settings: *oriel.store.Store = undefined;

fn setup() !void {
    settings = try oriel.store.Store.open(std.heap.smp_allocator, app.build.id, "settings");
}

pub const Commands = struct {
    pub fn get_theme(_: std.mem.Allocator) []const u8 {
        return settings.getString("theme") orelse "system";
    }

    pub fn set_theme(_: std.mem.Allocator, args: struct { theme: []const u8 }) !void {
        if (!std.mem.eql(u8, args.theme, "light") and !std.mem.eql(u8, args.theme, "dark") and
            !std.mem.eql(u8, args.theme, "system")) return error.InvalidTheme;
        try settings.set("theme", args.theme);
    }
};
```

Pass `.setup = setup` in `oriel.main`'s config. The returned string is
borrowed from the store and stays valid until `deinit`; the command's
result is serialized before the next call.

## [Batch several changes into one write]($heading.id('example-batch'))

```zig
var store = try oriel.store.Store.open(gpa, app.build.id, "settings");
defer store.deinit(); // saves (auto_save is back on)

store.auto_save = false;
try store.set("width", 1280);
try store.set("height", 800);
try store.set("recent", .{ "/home/me/a.txt", "/home/me/b.txt" });
store.auto_save = true;
try store.save(); // one atomic write
```

`auto_save` is a plain field, not guarded by the mutex: change it only
while no other thread uses that store.

## [Structured values]($heading.id('example-struct'))

`set` takes anything `std.json.Stringify` can write (structs, arrays,
optionals, enums); `get` returns the `std.json.Value`, which
`std.json.parseFromValue` turns back into a struct:

```zig
const Window = struct { x: i32, y: i32, docked: bool = false };

try store.set("palette", Window{ .x = 40, .y = 60 });

if (store.get("palette")) |v| {
    const parsed = try std.json.parseFromValue(Window, gpa, v, .{});
    defer parsed.deinit();
    std.log.info("palette at {d},{d}", .{ parsed.value.x, parsed.value.y });
}
```

## [A file outside the config directory]($heading.id('example-open-path'))

```zig
const dir = try oriel.paths.appData(gpa, .{ .name = app.build.id });
defer gpa.free(dir);
const path = try std.fs.path.join(gpa, &.{ dir, "library.json" });
defer gpa.free(path);
var lib = try oriel.store.Store.openPath(gpa, path); // the directory must exist
defer lib.deinit();
```

The showcase counts its launches with the store
(`examples/showcase/src/main.zig`, the `hello` store).

# [Reference]($heading.id('reference'))

## [`oriel.store`]($heading.id('zig-api'))

```zig
pub const available: bool;

pub const Store; // GenericStore(<this platform's backend>)

pub fn configDir(gpa: std.mem.Allocator, app_id: []const u8) ![]const u8;
pub fn dataDir(gpa: std.mem.Allocator, app_id: []const u8) ![]const u8;
pub fn cacheDir(gpa: std.mem.Allocator, app_id: []const u8) ![]const u8;

pub fn check(gpa: std.mem.Allocator, ctx: oriel.CheckContext) !oriel.Check;
pub const impl; // this platform's backend
pub const common; // GenericStore, validateAppId, buildAppPath
```

## [`Store`]($heading.id('store'))

| Declaration | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `open(gpa, app_id: []const u8, name: []const u8) !*Store` | Opens (or starts) `<configDir(app_id)>/<name>.json`; `.json` is added unless `name` already ends with it. Creates the directory. |
| `openPath(gpa, path: []const u8) !*Store` | Opens a store at any path. The directory must exist; the file needn't. |
| `deinit(self) void` | Saves (when `auto_save` is on, errors ignored) and frees the store. Every value `get` returned becomes invalid. |
| `get(self, key) ?std.json.Value` | The raw value, or null. |
| `getString(self, key) ?[]const u8` | The string, or null when missing or not a string. |
| `getInt(self, key, comptime T: type) ?T` | The integer cast to `T`, or null when missing, not an integer, or out of `T`'s range. |
| `getFloat(self, key, comptime T: type) ?T` | The number as `T` (integers convert), or null. |
| `getBool(self, key) ?bool` | The boolean, or null. |
| `has(self, key) bool` | Whether the key exists. |
| `set(self, key, value: anytype) !void` | Stores a copy of `value` (anything `std.json.Stringify` accepts, `std.json.Value` included) and, with `auto_save`, saves. |
| `delete(self, key) bool` | Removes the key; true if it was there. With `auto_save`, saves (a failed save is ignored). |
| `clear(self) !void` | Removes every key; with `auto_save`, saves. |
| `save(self) !void` | Writes the file now, atomically. |
| `auto_save: bool` | Default `true`. Not locked: set it while no other thread uses the store. |

**Values.** Strings, arrays and objects returned by the getters are
borrowed from the store's arena: valid until `deinit`, even after the key
is overwritten or deleted (the arena only grows; a store that is `set`
millions of times should be reopened now and then). Keys are compared
exactly; the order in the file is insertion order, with deletes moving the
last key into the hole.

**Errors.** `open` and `openPath`: allocation failures; the directory's
errors (Windows `error.KnownFolderNotFound`, `error.CreateDirectoryFailed`;
macOS and iOS `error.HomeNotSet`; Android `error.AppNotRunning` before the
runtime started); `error.InvalidAppId` / `error.EmptyAppId` from the app id
check; on macOS, iOS and Android `error.OpenFailed`, `error.ReadFailed` and
`error.StoreTooLarge` (over 16 MiB). Saving: `error.SaveFailed` (Linux,
Windows; Linux logs GLib's message), or on macOS, iOS and Android
`error.CreateTempFailed`, `error.WriteFailed`, `error.SyncFailed`,
`error.RenameFailed`.

**Threads.** Every method locks the store; a `*Store` may be used from any
thread. Opening the same file twice gives two independent stores.

## [Directories]($heading.id('directories'))

`configDir`, `dataDir` and `cacheDir` return `<base>/<app_id>`, created if
missing; the caller frees the path.

| | `configDir` (the store's files) | `dataDir` | `cacheDir` |
|---|---|---|---|
| Linux | `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/<id>` (`~/.config/<id>`) | `$XDG_DATA_HOME/<id>` (`~/.local/share/<id>`) | `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/<id>` (`~/.cache/<id>`) |
| Windows | `%APPDATA%\<id>` (roams with the profile) | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\<id>` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\<id>\cache` |
| macOS | `~/Library/Application Support/<id>` | the same as `configDir` | `~/Library/Caches/<id>` |
| iOS | `<container>/Library/Application Support/<id>` | the same as `configDir` | `<container>/Library/Caches/<id>` |
| Android | `<filesDir>/<id>` | the same as `configDir` | `<cacheDir>/<id>` |

For an app's own data and cache folders, use
[`oriel.paths`]($link.page('docs/paths')), which is always built and is
the same folder as `dataDir` / `cacheDir` everywhere but Android.

**App id rules** (`common.validateAppId`): not empty (`error.EmptyAppId`);
no `/`, `\`, `:`, `..`, NUL or control characters (`error.InvalidAppId`).
The id becomes a directory name.

## [Window geometry]($heading.id('window-geometry'))

A window with `.remember_geometry = true` (in `WindowOptions`) saves its
size and maximized state to the `window_geometry` store
(`<configDir>/window_geometry.json`, keys `<label>_width`,
`<label>_height`, `<label>_maximized`) and restores them when it is
created. With the store off, `remember_geometry` does nothing.

## [Smoke check]($heading.id('check'))

`check` writes, rereads and deletes a temporary store (in `/tmp`, the temp
directory, or the Android cache directory). `oriel.checkAll` runs it with
every enabled module's check.

# [Troubleshooting]($heading.id('troubleshooting'))

- **Settings were reset and a `.corrupt` file appeared.** The JSON didn't
  parse (edited by hand, or written by something else). The log has
  `failed to parse store file <path> (<error>); kept a copy at
  <path>.corrupt`. Fix the copy and move it back while the app is closed.
- **A value written in one place isn't seen in another.** Two `Store`s
  were opened on the same file; each has its own copy. Share one.
- **`oriel.store.Store is disabled`** at build time: the dependency has
  `.store = false`; turn it on or guard the use with
  `if (oriel.store.available)`.
- **`AppNotRunning` on Android.** The store was opened before the runtime
  handed over its directories; open it in `setup` or a command, not at
  comptime or from a global initializer.

